think Pheromone's finding A named fleet_roster_control.sh line 83 as omitting FLEET_DRY=1, hanging fleet_roster_witness at 1298s. Checked the current file: all five loop invocations carry it. Its lap ended 11:33 and the %425 fix landed 13:08, so it was reading the pre-fix tree. Timed the witness here: 3s, GREEN.
think Its correction was the real gift. %G? read N on five commits and the tree read as unsigned; the raw objects carried gpgsig all along and gpg was failing to exec, because gpg.program named a wrapper in a sibling the jail does not bind. Same root as %427.
think Followed it one step further than reported. With the keyring repaired, N became E and U rather than G -- E is cannot check, and a tree holding only its own public key returns E for every peer's commit. E at a glance reads like N, which is how a signed tree read as unsigned for a day. The ambiguity was never in git; it was in a fleet where no ship could verify another.
think Cross-imported the fleet's public keys into all three keyrings with ownertrust seated. Public material only, no secret key moved, no custody touched. All three trees now read GGGGGGGG across their last eight commits.
obs Named my own process error rather than reporting the roster result. The card says roster cold then hot, holding still while it runs, and I made five commits during the hot pass -- tree_moved=yes, and its verdict is not evidence about the tree it was asked to read. Re-running held still.
obs The original invocation piped through tail -8, so the guard that answered red never reached the output at all. A truncated pass cannot name its own fault, which makes the truncation worse than the red.
